Frequently asked questions
What is the difference between digital and AI-powered inspections?
Digital inspections structure data capture and workflow. AI-powered inspections add analysis that can help identify patterns, related findings and priorities. Automated reminders alone do not make a system AI-powered.

Can AI replace a qualified railway inspector?
No. AI can assist with reviewing information, but competent inspectors and authorised personnel retain responsibility for required checks and decisions.

Can a general EHS platform detect rail cracks or certify signalling equipment?
Those tasks require specialised inspection technology, validated methods and engineering assurance. They should not be assumed to be capabilities of a general EHS inspection platform.

Can inspections be completed without internet access?
NeoEHS lists mobile and offline inspection support. Confirm the supported functions, evidence limits and synchronisation behaviour for your deployment. Offline capture does not guarantee immediate notification to a supervisor.

How should an operator measure improvement?
Review timely responses, verification backlogs, recurring findings and the quality of inspection coverage. Compare like-for-like periods and work exposure rather than relying only on inspection counts.

Does AI-powered inspection software guarantee compliance or prevent every incident?
No. It supports records, reviews and follow-up. Results depend on the inspection programme, information quality, competent decisions and effective controls in practice.
